---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
		<style>
			.about-hero {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(18rem, 0.85fr);
				gap: 1rem;
				align-items: start;
			}

			.about-panel,
			.about-story,
			.about-principles,
			.about-stack {
				padding: 1.4rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
				background: var(--bg-elevated);
				box-shadow: var(--shadow-xl);
			}

			.about-story,
			.about-principles,
			.about-stack {
				margin-top: 1rem;
			}

			.about-panel p,
			.about-story p,
			.about-principles p,
			.about-stack p {
				margin-top: 0.85rem;
				line-height: 1.85;
				color: var(--text-body);
			}

			.about-list {
				display: grid;
				gap: 0.75rem;
				list-style: none;
				padding: 0;
				margin: 1rem 0 0;
			}

			.about-list li {
				padding: 0.95rem 1rem;
				border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
				border: 1px solid rgba(180, 208, 255, 0.08);
				background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
			}

			.about-list strong {
				display: block;
				margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
			}

			.about-list span {
				color: var(--text-muted);
			}

			.about-signals {
				display: grid;
				gap: 0.75rem;
			}

			.about-signal {
				padding: 0.95rem 1rem;
				border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
				border: 1px solid rgba(180, 208, 255, 0.08);
				background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
			}

			.about-signal strong {
				display: block;
				margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
			}

			@media (max-width: 1024px) {
				.about-hero {
					grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="about-hero">
				<div class="about-panel">
					<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
					<h1>Engineering with a systems view, not a feature checklist.</h1>
					<p>
						This portfolio is built to signal how I work: I care about maintainable architecture, clear
						operating behavior, and the ability to ship confidently without creating future cleanup.
					</p>
					<ul class="about-list">
						<li>
							<strong>Strong systems thinking</strong>
							<span>Understand the boundaries before styling the screens.</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Security-conscious delivery</strong>
							<span>Treat permissions, trust, and failure states as first-class UX.</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Scalability awareness</strong>
							<span>Prefer patterns that support growth without turning the codebase brittle.</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<aside class="about-stack">
					<p class="panel-label">What this site demonstrates</p>
					<div class="about-signals">
						<div class="about-signal">
							<strong>Intentional UI</strong>
							<span>Premium presentation without sacrificing clarity or performance.</span>
						</div>
						<div class="about-signal">
							<strong>Operational maturity</strong>
							<span>Content, metadata, and routing are arranged to stay easy to maintain.</span>
						</div>
						<div class="about-signal">
							<strong>Deployment-ready</strong>
							<span>Configured for GitHub Pages with clean static output.</span>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>

			<section class="about-story">
				<div class="section-heading">
					<p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>
					<h2>How I think about frontend ownership</h2>
				</div>
				<p>
					The strongest frontend teams behave like platform teams. They reduce ambiguity, publish stable
					interfaces for other engineers, and make the path to safe change obvious. That is the standard I
					try to bring into every surface I touch.
				</p>
				<p>
					I tend to favor small abstractions with clear purpose, documentation that helps future maintainers,
					and visual systems that feel deliberate rather than decorative. A good experience should be calm,
					fast, and easy to reason about under pressure.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="about-principles">
				<div class="section-heading">
					<p class="eyebrow">Principles</p>
					<h2>What I optimize for</h2>
				</div>
				<div class="card-grid">
					<div class="card">
						<p class="meta">System design</p>
						<h3>Clear boundaries</h3>
						<p>State, data flow, and responsibility should be visible in the code and understandable in review.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="card">
						<p class="meta">Delivery</p>
						<h3>Predictable release behavior</h3>
						<p>When the product changes, operational risk should stay low and rollback paths should stay obvious.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="card">
						<p class="meta">Maintainability</p>
						<h3>Future-friendly code</h3>
						<p>Good interfaces lower the cost of the next feature, the next incident, and the next teammate.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>